From d675e4a1164de676f3a64f1b041340260bd32a8e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sungsu Ahn <sungsu_ahn@korea.ac.kr>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 22:08:28 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 02/51] nr: shared log across processes (header in SCR, entries
 in LNR)

- Log::new_in_place builds or attaches to a log whose header and entries
  live in caller memory; init registers all replicas up front
  (next = n+1), attach writes nothing and checks the header.
  register_at(tkn) hands out the fixed token rid+1.
- NodeReplicated: log is &'static (never dropped), replicas is
  Vec<Option<Box<Replica>>> with only node_id local in shared mode;
  every indexing site goes through local(rid) [V3]. A stuck remote
  replica is waited for (ltail no longer pins head, or caught up) with a
  timeout that aborts; GcFailed returns the response only after that
  [V3]. log_sync_numa skips remote replicas; log_sync_local added.
- Replica::exec_notify factored out of combine; exec (try_sync/sync)
  uses it, so log-sync replays clear change_notif and flush slots [V4].
- execute_anchor/execute_locked_anchor store change_notif while holding
  the read guard [C3].
- Log entries span 128 B: writer flushes all lines, sfence, publishes
  alivef, flushes its line; reader invalidates all lines [V8].
- ffi: create_node_replicated_shared (no-op affinity, background log-sync
  thread, stuck timeout), nr_log_layout, stop_log_sync,
  NR_LOG_ENTRY_SIZE with a compile-time check; NUMA asserts removed.
- ffi/port_tests.rs: two in-process nodes over one in-place log.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
